#: ../../../plugin-api.rst:74
msgid ""
"Your plugin may modify either value and those new values will be used as "
"input to the highlighting engine.  If you add a ``result`` key to the object "
"that result will be returned as the overall result and the internal "
"highlighting code will never even be called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../plugin-api.rst:79
msgid ""
"If you're plugin plans to make its own recursive calls to ``highlight`` "
"you'll need to manually handle this. Each time ``highlight`` is called your "
"plugin callbacks will also be called - making it easy to get into an "
"infinite loop. You'll likely need to use a class based plugin and add a "
"guard so that your plugin code is only triggered on the initial call to "
"``highlight`` and not on any internal calls your plugin itself is making."
msgstr ""

